The [architecture](docs/architecture.md) explains module boundaries. Dated
producers and their paths are retained because recorded experiments hash their
actual code and inputs. They are evidence archives, not competing scoring
interfaces. The pre-consolidation documentation is preserved in the
[review archive](analysis/remaining_review_20261022_01/documentation_before/README.md).

In the recorded QM Python environment, run the unit/regression suite with
`python -m pytest -q`. A minimal CPU boundary check uses
`python -m pytest tests/unit/test_refactor_boundaries.py -q` after installing
`.[test]`. GPU integrations require an allocation and explicit
`METAG_RUN_GPU_TESTS=1`; full test collection requires the optional QM Python
packages in modules that import the energy backend.

Current evidence and remaining scientific gates are indexed in the
[review work record](analysis/remaining_review_20261022_01/WORK_STATUS.txt) and
[current review response](manuscript/evidence/review_response.md).
The [official-profile status](analysis/official_default_20261024_01/WORK_STATUS_CURRENT.json)
identifies completed evaluations, active audit jobs and their exact source identities.
The paper separates its physical component diagnostics, historical biochemical
scores and external-source evaluation. Reference, model, sampling and condition
limitations accompany each result; source dates alone do not prove a holdout.

